ousAt gamma.val t and proves the scaled c^4/c^2 polynomial inequality. Its type does not require c>0; positivity is needed here to divide by c^2. This source correspondence does not identify the SKSupport and SKValue models, pass third time derivatives through a shrinking-plateau limit, or establish the smooth-density corollary as an exported formal conclusion. No fresh Lean build, elaborated dependency extraction, Comparator result or independent semantic acceptance is recorded.","citation_ids":["support_fixed_time_source","support_fixed_time_polynomials","support_regularity_source","support_diffusion_source","scalar-r2-26-cite-smooth-positive-density"],"evidence_ids":["fixed_time_spatial_warrant_20261025"],"id":"support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity","kind":"claim","label":"Spatial coercivity at a positive continuity time","locator":"Long record, fixed-time-coercivity: fixed-time estimate and shrinking-plateau argument; corresponding source SampleJets.lean:135–143","source_id":"authored_long_comparisons_20261024","statement":"For every admissible manuscript coefficient gamma in U, every 0<t<1 at which gamma is continuous, and c=gamma(t)>0, let a=Phi_xx(t,X_t), b=Phi_xxx(t,X_t), d=Phi_xxxx(t,X_t) along its controlled diffusion. Then E[d^2-12*c*a*b^2+6*c^2*a^4] >= (c^2/1000)*E[a^4]. No minimizer or constant-neighborhood premise is required.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.constant_curvature","id":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/edges/%5B%22scalar.constant_curvature%22%2C%22support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/edges/%5B%22scalar.constant_curvatu